oh-my-ztty on Arch Linux
========================

Run `omztty terminal` to open the system-packaged ztty terminal, or `omztty shell` to use
its zsh preset in an existing terminal. `omztty doctor` checks the installation.
No background service starts during package installation.

The package owns /usr/lib/oh-my-ztty and /usr/bin/omztty. The terminal comes from the separate ztty package. Other bundled component
commands remain private to the suite, so separate ssmcp, zdot and zfetch
packages can coexist. If a previous per-user installation
appears first in PATH, use /usr/bin/omztty to select this package explicitly.

Configuration is adopted only when you request it as your ordinary user:

    omztty config init
    omztty config plan
    omztty config apply --backup

Existing conflicting files are backed up by the explicit apply command.
Personal additions belong in ~/.config/oh-my-ztty/local.zsh. The editable
profile is at ~/.config/oh-my-ztty/profile; XDG paths are respected.

Update the package with your AUR helper, for example:

    yay -Syu oh-my-ztty-bin

After an update, run `omztty config refresh` to update unchanged shipped
defaults while preserving personal edits. Review its updated/preserved file
report. Package installation and upgrades do not edit home files.

Before removing the package, restore an adopted home profile if desired:

    omztty config remove
    sudo pacman -R oh-my-ztty-bin

Removing the package preserves personal configuration, backups and history.
The built-in updater and uninstaller direct package users to the package
manager; they do not change pacman-owned files.
